   Hmm, but careful: the regex engine evaluates lookbehinds... the overall match at position p requires ALL lookbehind conditions. If positive lookbehind fails, no match regardless. So yes, only positions where s[p-1] ∈ {'.', '?'} matter, and there the `.` matches fine.

   Also `\s` in the regex: matches a single ASCII whitespace char: [ \t\n\x0B\f\r]. Note: the matched character s[p] must be one of these.

