   Now, one more subtlety: how does the regex engine scan? matcher.find() finds the leftmost match, then continues from end of previous match. Since matches are single characters, it just scans positions left to right. Since our conditions are all local (depend on p-4..p), and the match length is 1, consecutive matches don't overlap. So: iterate p from 0 to len-1; if conditions hold, record match at [p, p+1).

